### worker-service — example requests
# worker/worker-service-with-loco — "person-style" layout (src/api/rest/).
# Envelope: {"success":bool,"data":...,"error":{"code","message","details"}}
# — data/error ALWAYS both present, identical shape to person's (src/api/mod.rs).
# Gated by WORKER_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082
@workerId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@otherWorkerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@assessmentId = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token (its own AuthUser
# extractor, not gated by WORKER_REQUIRE_AUTH) — curl-verified: 401s
# "missing authorization header" with no token even though the blanket
# guard is off. See person.http for the same pattern and the compose
# gap (no WORKER_PASETO_KEYS_URL wired to authentication-service).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a worker — minimal valid body (mirrors person's Human Name +
# gender requirement).
# @name createWorker
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "name": { "use": "official", "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Get the created worker back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}


### Search workers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/search?q=Smith&limit=10&offset=0


### Update a worker
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": { "use": "official", "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada", "Jane"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Probabilistic + deterministic match
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/match
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": { "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Explicit duplicate check
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": { "family": "Smith", "given": ["Ada"] },
  "birth_date": "1990-05-15",
  "gender": "female"
}


### Batch deduplicate
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/deduplicate


### Review queue — list pending candidate pairs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/review-queue?status=pending


### Review queue — decide a pending item
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/review-queue/{{reviewId}}/decision
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "status": "confirmed" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate workers (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_id": "{{workerId}}", "duplicate_id": "{{otherWorkerId}}" }


### Cross-service link — assert same_identity back to the person record,
# and employed_by to an organization.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/links
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "same_identity", "to_ref": "person:{{otherWorkerId}}" }


### List this worker's outbound links
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/links


### Record a workforce assessment (aptitude / personality / psychometric /
# selection — worker-only capability, per-scale results + score bands).
# GOTCHA (curl-verified): the assessment endpoints bypass the crate's
# usual ApiResponse envelope entirely and return the created assessment
# BARE with 201 Created (src/api/rest/assessments.rs — `Json(created)`,
# not the ApiResponse wrapper every other worker.http request uses).
# @name createAssessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/assessments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "category": "psychometric",
  "instrument": "Numerical Reasoning Inventory",
  "provider": "Test Publisher",
  "status": "completed",
  "administered_on": "2026-01-15",
  "results": [
    { "scale": "numerical_reasoning", "raw_score": 41.0, "max_score": 50.0, "percentile": 82.0, "narrative": "strong under time pressure" }
  ]
}


### Get one assessment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/assessments/{{assessmentId}}


### Derived assessment profile for this worker (masked under ABAC)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/assessment-profile


### Masked view
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}/audit


### FHIR R5 — read this worker as a Practitioner resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Practitioner/{{workerId}}


### Delete (soft-delete) a worker
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/workers/{{workerId}}
